    <h1>What AttoLang learns from Microsoft Orleans</h1>
    <LogPrompt prompt={prompt} label="The engineering question" headingTag="span" />
    <div class="log-entry-meta"><span>Authored by <strong>Alex Mills</strong></span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><time datetime="2026-11-01">November 1, 2026</time></div>
    <p class="log-entry-intro">The best idea in Orleans is not that actors run in a cluster. It is that <strong>an actor's logical identity does not have to be the same thing as a live object in memory</strong>. AttoLang can build on that insight while retaining explicit ownership, bounded mailboxes, supervision, and native compilation.</p>
